"kill",
"• BepInEx (+ changelog.txt, doorstop_config.ini & winhttp.dll)\n• PeakArchipelago folder (Archipelago.MultiClient.Net.dll, energylinkstore.peakbundle, Newtonsoft.Json.dll, PeakArchipelago.dll & YamlDotNet.dll)\n• peak.apworld",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"When you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, peak.apworld will be installed and moved into the custom_worlds folder within the Archipelago Launcher directory. BepInEx will then be downloaded into the PEAK game directory, along with the PeakArchipelago folder, which will be placed in plugins.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"PEAK is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file (peak.apworld). When the apworld is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once everything is set up, you should be able to see an Archipelago icon in the bottom-left corner in the main menu. If you do see it, open a lobby, press ESCAPE and there should be a 'Archipelago' button, click it.\n\nIn the 'SERVER' field, enter archipelago.gg.\n\nIn 'PORT' enter the room’s 5-digit port number. You can find this number on the website after creating a new room.\n\nIn 'SLOT NAME', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nThe 'PASSWORD' field is optional. If the host did not set one, leave it blank.\n\nFinally, click 'Connect' and then, you can start a new run!\n\nYou can also go in the 'LINKS' tab to change the AP rules and the 'TRACKER' tab to follow your progress in the Archipelago world.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"You have 2 revert options, both can't be enabled at the same time.\n\nIf you use the 'Clear AP Mods' option it will only delete the mods that are required for PEAK Archipelago.\n\nIf you use the 'Full Clear BepInEx' option it will delete everything related to BepInEx and mods. If other mods are detected an additionnal confirmation will appear.",
